1
00:00:21,176 --> 00:00:27,176
Tokyo Mater is a animation, comedy, family film directed by John Lasseter.

2
00:00:42,352 --> 00:00:48,352
A routine tow lands Mater in Tokyo, where he is challenged to a drift-style
race against a nefarious gang leader and his posse of ninjas.

3
00:01:03,529 --> 00:01:09,529
With the help of his friend, 'Dragon' Lightning McQueen, and some special modifications, Mater
attempts to drift to victory and become Tow-ke-O Mater, King of all Drifters.

4
00:01:24,705 --> 00:01:30,705
Mater (voice), played by Larry the Cable Guy.

5
00:01:45,882 --> 00:01:51,882
Lightning McQueen (voice), played by Keith Ferguson.

6
00:02:07,058 --> 00:02:13,058
Tia (voice), played by Elissa Knight.

7
00:02:28,235 --> 00:02:34,235
Guido (voice), played by Guido Quaroni.

8
00:02:49,411 --> 00:02:55,411
Additional Voice Talent (voice), played by Lori Alan.

9
00:03:10,588 --> 00:03:16,588
Additional Voice Talent (voice), played by Mickie McGowan.

10
00:03:31,764 --> 00:03:37,764
Cars Toons is an American animated short series based on the Cars franchise.

11
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:58,941
It features Lightning McQueen, Mater, and their friends in
comedic antics and adventures canonical to the films.

12
00:04:14,117 --> 00:04:20,117
Larry the Cable Guy reprises his role as Mater while Keith Ferguson replaces Owen Wilson as the voice
of Lightning McQueen until "The Radiator Springs 500 ½", when Wilson reprises his role.

13
00:04:35,294 --> 00:04:41,294
The series premiered on October 27, 2008, with "Rescue Squad
Mater" on Disney Channel, Toon Disney and ABC Family.

14
00:04:56,470 --> 00:05:02,470
Not exclusive to television, the shorts were also released
on home media and/or as theatrical shorts.

15
00:05:17,647 --> 00:05:23,647
The series ended on May 20, 2014, with "The Radiator Springs 500 ½".

16
00:05:38,823 --> 00:05:44,823
The tone is lighthearted.
